Subject: [PATCH] feat(sync): v2 - two-key trust with signed rotation chain,
 future-skew limit, compromise taint

- keys: genesis active+standby pinned in /etc; rotations keys/rotation-<n>.json signed ONLY by the standby,
  chain persisted in lock.json cora_keys and required to start from the /etc pins
- manifests: refused if signed by the standby or a revoked key; trusted-comment timestamp max 24 h ahead
- replay counter resets per key epoch, so a poisoned future timestamp cannot pin a node
- compromised_after: tainted community lists and last-good purged at once; next new-key manifest applies over caps
- cora-blocklist sync --standby-pubkey; dispatcher test for bare sync-rollback
- tests/test_sync_rotation.py (34); every rule mutation-checked; docs/blocklist-sync.md runbooks
